    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "437cd944477d248f790980dc6f6da8af2f1dc7c66b282a2702995689acd58541",
      "text": "After breakfast, head to Los Glaciares National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, to visit Perito Moreno Glacier.\n\nOn the way, your guide will explain what makes the national park distinctive and why the glacier matters to the ecosystem. The first stop is at the walkways and viewing platforms. From here, you can see the wall of ice clearly and watch the glacier move.\n\nFrom time to time, large pieces of ice break off Perito Moreno and crash into the water. Even when it seems still, the glacier is constantly changing, so you’ll spend a good part of the day watching it from the platforms. After the walk, continue by bus through the park for different views of the glacier, lake and surrounding mountains.\n\nWe recommend bringing a packed lunch. You can also have lunch at the park restaurant.\n\n**Ice trekking on Perito Moreno Glacier**\n\nAn optional trek on the glacier costs $360 per person and includes a cocktail served with ice from Perito Moreno.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw8xmmzc-4ws6bwp2vxe",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      }
